        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bound model run image reads with per-file and aggregate budget",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `readModelRunImageFiles` function in `src/cli/capability-cli/model.ts` reads image files for model run capability. It used a TOCTOU-prone pattern: `statSync(path)` to check file size (100 MiB per-file cap + 500 MiB aggregate budget), then a separate `fs.readFile(path)` to read the content. Between the stat and the read, the file could be swapped with a much larger one, defeating the size cap.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nModel run files are user-supplied inputs that could be symlink-swapped or replaced between the stat validation and the read. While the per-file and aggregate budgets provide defense-in-depth, the TOCTOU window means an attacker who can control the file at the path can bypass the per-file cap. Opening the file first and operating on the same descriptor eliminates this race.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the path-based `statSync` + `await fs.readFile` pattern with descriptor-bound reads using `fs.promises.open`:\n\n```typescript\nconst handle = await fs.open(resolvedPath, \"r\");\ntry {\n  const stat = await handle.stat();\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(\"not a regular file\");\n  if (stat.size > MAX_MODEL_RUN_IMAGE_BYTES) throw new Error(\"file too large\");\n  budget.remaining -= stat.size;\n  return await handle.readFile();\n} finally {\n  await handle.close();\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle` — `stat()` and `readFile()` both operate on the same descriptor\n- `try/finally` guarantees `handle.close()` even when exceptions are thrown\n- Per-file 100 MiB cap and 500 MiB aggregate budget are preserved from the original implementation\n- `import { statSync }` was removed as no longer needed\n- Sequential processing (already in original) is retained\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `statSync(path)` → TOCTOU race: file could be swapped before read | → fd pins the inode; race impossible |\n| Normal model run with valid files → works | → works (unchanged) |\n| Per-file 100 MiB cap + 500 MiB aggregate budget | → preserved, now without TOCTOU |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 109 capability-cli tests pass:**\n\n```\n ✓ |cli| src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts (109 tests) 3133ms\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  109 passed (109)\n```\n\nThe descriptor-bound pattern is the standard fix for TOCTOU file races — the fd pins the specific inode, preventing substitution between validation and consumption.",
